{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attack by supplying a cloud metadata service IP address (169.254.169.254) to the preview API endpoint to exfiltrate sensitive instance data. The HTTP 200 status code in the log indicates that the server successfully processed the request and potentially returned the sensitive metadata back to the user.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and allow-listing for URLs accepted by the preview endpoint.",
    "Block access to internal network ranges and link-local IP addresses (such as 169.254.169.254) at the application or firewall level.",
    "Enforce IMDSv2 on cloud instances and restrict metadata service access to mitigate the impact of potential SSRF vulnerabilities."
  ]
}
